  "seamGemChance": 0.3,
  "_laserGapComment": "A mining laser by its gap: its grade minus the rock's tier (the system's Mk), clamped to +2. `work` scales how fast it works the rock (so how often chunks come: one every chunkUnits worked), `keep` the share of what it works that it keeps. A grade behind is a little slower and loses a fifth; two behind, slower again and loses two fifths; further behind it can't mine the rock. Each laser mines on its own (no crowding): what limits a ship's lasers is the power to run them (a Mining Laser draws most of a Cell Reactor: models.json).",
  "laserGap": {
    "2": {
      "work": 1.3,
      "keep": 1
    },
    "1": {
      "work": 1.2,
      "keep": 1
    },
    "0": {
      "work": 1,
      "keep": 1
    },
    "-1": {
      "work": 0.85,
      "keep": 0.8
    },
    "-2": {
      "work": 0.7,
      "keep": 0.6
    }
  },
  "_gunsComment": "Guns (every tool but a mining tool: tools[k].mining, or a mining laser) mine soft rock only (hardness 1). They work it at about a Mk I mining laser's pace: damage x tools[kind].yield / damagePerUnit, and past refDps damage a second on the rock the pace grows only with its square root (a starter's two Pips, 112 a second, about 0.7 rock units a second like the laser; a gunship twice that, about 1.4x). They keep `keep` of the common ores, keepOther times that of anything else (gems too), and keepByTier times that again by the rock's tier: a Mk I laser gets about three times the ore off Mk I rock, from chunks as often.",
  "guns": {
    "refDps": 112,
    "keep": 0.32,
    "common": [
      "iron_ore",
      "nickel_ore",
      "silicate",
      "ice"
    ],
    "keepOther": 0.5,
    "keepByTier": {
      "1": 1,
      "2": 0.4,
      "3": 0.15,
      "4": 0.08,
      "5": 0.05
    }
  },
  "_outliersComment": "Outliers: about one belt rock in 130 is 3.5-4.5x its size. Mining it (or blasting it) breaks it down through `stages` (its size as a fraction of the first), each a fresh smaller rock carrying the ore that's left, until the last breaks up. `common` of them are a lump of common ore: each ore's weight x its boost (unlisted ores x rare).",
